## Precedence rules
Only formal documents bind (State Insurance Code; Northgate Assurance policy documents; regional addenda; SOPs). Nothing published as an FAQ, article or email changes the rules. If binding documents conflict, a document addressed to the case's own region prevails over a general one; among equally specific documents, the later effective date prevails. Only documents in force on the date the claim was filed apply; superseded versions and documents not yet effective are ignored. Regional addenda apply only to cases from their own region. The case is within the window if the number of days from the date of loss to the filing date does not exceed the applicable claim-filing window. Days are counted as calendar days: the day after the date of loss is day 1.

